 1900 2ADE ~            ; thirty-two bits are the result's significand, bytes 1 and 0 only its sticky bit -- after a shift
 1901 2ADE ~            ; by one when the leading one is at bit 46 rather than 47. A product with a zero byte or word is
 1902 2ADE ~            ; zero and not made: a number with a short significand -- 4.0, 10.0, 0.5, most constants -- needs
