 4578 2BD2 ~            .general:
 4579 2BD2 ~                ; A divisor of 32768 or more: still a byte of the quotient at a time, the same non-restoring
 4580 2BD2 ~                ; steps with the next byte of the dividend added after each pass, but the remainder no longer
 4581 2BD2 ~                ; fits sixteen bits. Below 2^23 it is twenty-four, in E:HL, and the quotient's byte comes
 4582 2BD2 ~                ; together in D behind a sentinel bit that drops out at the eighth step; from 2^23 it is
 4583 2BD2 ~                ; thirty-two, DE:HL, and the quotient's byte waits in rt_lo. The divisor's low word is in BC,
 4584 2BD2 ~                ; to add; the rest of it, and its negative to take it off, in memory -- -d in rt_r, which the
 4585 2BD2 ~                ; remainder replaces at the end. As the 16-bit passes do, the carry tells which way the
 4586 2BD2 ~                ; remainder went, which holds while the doubled remainder fits: hence the limits 2^23 and
 4587 2BD2 ~                ; 2^31. From 2^31 the quotient is 0 or 1.
